{"id":"mahabharata-3-134","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":134,"title":"चतुस्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 134 · Ashtavakra defeats Bandin","summary":{"en":"Ashtavakra and Bandin compete in verses on numbers from one to thirteen; Bandin falters, and Ashtavakra completes the verse. Bandin reveals that he is Varuna's son and had sent the defeated Brahmins to his father's sacrifice; Kahoda returns from the waters, and bathing in the Samanga, Ashtavakra's limbs become straight.","kn":"ಅಷ್ಟಾವಕ್ರ ಬಂದಿಯರು ಒಂದರಿಂದ ಹದಿಮೂರರವರೆಗಿನ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆಗಳ ಪದ್ಯಸ್ಪರ್ಧೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಬಂದಿ ತಡವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅಷ್ಟಾವಕ್ರನು ಪದ್ಯ ಪೂರ್ಣಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಾನು ವರುಣನ ಮಗ, ಸೋತ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರನ್ನು ತಂದೆಯ ಯಜ್ಞಕ್ಕೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸಿದ್ದೆ ಎಂದು ಬಂದಿ ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕಹೋಡನು ನೀರಿನಿಂದ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಸಮಂಗೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸ್ನಾನಮಾಡಿ ಅಷ್ಟಾವಕ್ರನ ಅಂಗಗಳು ನೇರವಾಗುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"अष्टावक्र और बन्दी एक से तेरह तक की संख्याओं पर पद्यों में प्रतिस्पर्धा करते हैं; बन्दी अटक जाता है और अष्टावक्र पद्य पूरा करते हैं। बन्दी बताता है कि वह वरुण का पुत्र है और हारे हुए ब्राह्मणों को पिता के यज्ञ में भेजता था; कहोड जल से लौटते हैं, और समङ्गा में स्नान से अष्टावक्र के अंग सीधे हो जाते हैं।","te":"అష్టావక్రుడు, వంది ఒకటి నుండి పదమూడు వరకు సంఖ్యలపై పద్యాలలో పోటీపడతారు; వంది తడబడతాడు, అష్టావక్రుడు పద్యాన్ని పూర్తి చేస్తాడు. తాను వరుణుని కుమారుడనని, ఓడిన బ్రాహ్మణులను తండ్రి యజ్ఞానికి పంపేవాడినని వంది వెల్లడిస్తాడు; కహోడుడు నీటి నుండి తిరిగివస్తాడు, సమంగలో స్నానంతో అష్టావక్రుని అవయవాలు తిన్నగా అవుతాయి.","ta":"அஷ்டாவக்ரனும் வந்தியும் ஒன்று முதல் பதின்மூன்று வரையிலான எண்கள் பற்றிய பாடல்களில் போட்டியிடுகிறார்கள்; வந்தி தடுமாற, அஷ்டாவக்ரன் பாடலை நிறைவு செய்கிறான். தான் வருணனின் மகன், தோற்ற அந்தணர்களைத் தந்தையின் யாகத்துக்கு அனுப்பினேன் என்று வந்தி வெளிப்படுத்துகிறான்; கஹோடர் நீரிலிருந்து திரும்ப, ஸமங்கையில் நீராடியதும் அஷ்டாவக்ரனின் உறுப்புகள் நேராகின்றன.","ml":"അഷ്ടാവക്രനും ബന്ദിയും ഒന്നുമുതൽ പതിമൂന്നുവരെയുള്ള സംഖ്യകളെക്കുറിച്ച് ശ്ലോകങ്ങളിൽ മത്സരിക്കുന്നു; ബന്ദി പതറുമ്പോൾ അഷ്ടാവക്രൻ ശ്ലോകം പൂർത്തിയാക്കുന്നു. താൻ വരുണന്റെ പുത്രനാണെന്നും തോറ്റ ബ്രാഹ്മണരെ പിതാവിന്റെ യാഗത്തിലേക്ക് അയച്ചതാണെന്നും ബന്ദി വെളിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; ജലത്തിൽനിന്ന് കഹോഡൻ തിരിച്ചെത്തുന്നു, സമംഗയിൽ സ്നാനം ചെയ്തപ്പോൾ അഷ്ടാവക്രന്റെ അവയവങ്ങൾ നേരെയാകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.134; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अत्रोग्रसेनसमितेषु राज-\nन्समागतेष्वप्रतिमेषु राजसु ।\nन वै विवित्सान्तरमस्ति वादिनां\nमहाजले हंसनिनादिनामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, among these peerless kings gathered in an assembly like Ugrasena's, there is no room for rivals in debate, as with swans calling over a great expanse of water."}},{"n":2,"text":"न मेऽद्य वक्ष्यस्यतिवादिमानि-\nन्ग्लहं प्रपन्नः सरितामिवागमः ।\nहुताशनस्येव समिद्धतेजसः\nस्थिरो भवस्वेह ममाद्य बन्दिन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bandin, you will not now speak boastfully to me, a wager before you, as a river does not speak to the sea. Stand firm here today against me, as one stands before a fire in full blaze."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"व्याघ्रं शयानं प्रति मा प्रबोधय\nआशीविषं सृक्किणी लेलिहानम् ।\nपदाहतस्येव शिरोऽभिहत्य\nनादष्टो वै मोक्ष्यसे तन्निबोध ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not rouse a sleeping tiger, nor a venomous snake licking the corners of its mouth. Like one struck by a foot, you will not escape unbitten by striking its head. Know this."}},{"n":4,"text":"यो वै दर्पात्संहननोपपन्नः\nसुदुर्बलः पर्वतमाविहन्ति ।\nतस्यैव पाणिः सनखो विशीर्यते\nन चैव शैलस्य हि दृश्यते व्रणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A weak man who in pride and with a strong frame strikes a mountain has only his hand and nails shattered, and no wound is seen on the rock."}},{"n":5,"text":"सर्वे राज्ञो मैथिलस्य मैनाकस्येव पर्वताः ।\nनिकृष्टभूता राजानो वत्सा अनदुहो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings are to the king of Mithila as the mountains are to Mainaka, and the other kings are mean, like calves of a bullock."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अष्टावक्रः समितौ गर्जमानो\nजातक्रोधो बन्दिनमाह राजन् ।\nउक्ते वाक्ये चोत्तरं मे ब्रवीहि\nवाक्यस्य चाप्युत्तरं ते ब्रवीमि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring in the assembly, Ashtavakra, angry, said to Bandin, king: \"Answer my statement when I have spoken, and I shall answer yours.\""}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"एक एवाग्निर्बहुधा समिध्यते\nएकः सूर्यः सर्वमिदं प्रभासते ।\nएको वीरो देवराजो निहन्ता\nयमः पितॄणामीश्वरश्चैक एव ॥","meaning":{"en":"One fire alone is kindled in many ways. One sun lights all this. One hero is the king of the gods, the slayer. One alone is Yama, lord of the fathers."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"द्वाविन्द्राग्नी चरतो वै सखायौ\nद्वौ देवर्षी नारदः पर्वतश्च ।\nद्वावश्विनौ द्वे च रथस्य चक्रे\nभार्यापती द्वौ विहितौ विधात्रा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two walk as friends: Indra and Agni. Two are the divine seers, Narada and Parvata. Two are the Ashvins. Two are the wheels of a chariot. The Creator ordained a pair, husband and wife."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"त्रिः सूयते कर्मणा वै प्रजेयं\nत्रयो युक्ता वाजपेयं वहन्ति ।\nअध्वर्यवस्त्रिषवणानि तन्वते\nत्रयो लोकास्त्रीणि ज्योतींषि चाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three times creatures are born by action. Three yoked horses draw the Vajapeya. The Adhvaryus perform the three pressings. Three are the worlds, and three lights are spoken of."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"चतुष्टयं ब्राह्मणानां निकेतं\nचत्वारो युक्ता यज्ञमिमं वहन्ति ।\nदिशश्चतस्रश्चतुरश्च वर्णा-\nश्चतुष्पदा गौरपि शश्वदुक्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Four is the dwelling of brahmins. Four yoked animals bear this sacrifice. There are four quarters, four classes, and the cow is always said to have four feet."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"पञ्चाग्नयः पञ्चपदा च पङ्क्ति-\nर्यज्ञाः पञ्चैवाप्यथ पञ्चेन्द्रियाणि ।\nदृष्टा वेदे पञ्चचूडाश्च पञ्च\nलोके ख्यातं पञ्चनदं च पुण्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Five are the fires, and the line of verse has five feet. Five are the sacrifices, and five the senses. Five tufts are seen in the Veda, and the holy Panchanada, the river of five streams, is famed in the world."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"षडाधाने दक्षिणामाहुरेके\nषडेवेमे ऋतवः कालचक्रम् ।\nषडिन्द्रियाण्युत षट्कृत्तिकाश्च\nषट्साद्यस्काः सर्ववेदेषु दृष्टाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some say that six cows are the fee at the laying of the fires. Six are the seasons, the wheel of time. Six are the senses, and six the Krittikas. Six sacrificial days are seen in all the Vedas."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"सप्त ग्राम्याः पशवः सप्त वन्याः\nसप्त छन्दांसि क्रतुमेकं वहन्ति ।\nसप्तर्षयः सप्त चाप्यर्हणानि\nसप्ततन्त्री प्रथिता चैव वीणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seven are the domestic animals and seven the wild. Seven metres carry a single sacrifice. Seven are the seers, seven the offerings of honour, and the lute with seven strings is renowned."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अष्टौ शाणाः शतमानं वहन्ति\nतथाष्टपादः शरभः सिंहघाती ।\nअष्टौ वसूञ्शुश्रुम देवतासु\nयूपश्चाष्टास्रिर्विहितः सर्वयज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eight shana weights make a shatamana. The eight-footed sharabha kills the lion. We have heard of eight Vasus among the gods, and the sacrificial post of every sacrifice is made with eight corners."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"नवैवोक्ताः सामिधेन्यः पितॄणां\nतथा प्राहुर्नवयोगं विसर्गम् ।\nनवाक्षरा बृहती संप्रदिष्टा\nनवयोगो गणनामेति शश्वत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nine are the kindling verses for the fathers. Nine-fold is the release of creation, they say. The Brihati metre is declared to have nine syllables, and the nine-fold union is always counted."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"दशा दशोक्ताः पुरुषस्य लोके\nसहस्रमाहुर्दश पूर्णं शतानि ।\nदशैव मासान्बिभ्रति गर्भवत्यो\nदशेरका दश दाशा दशार्णाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ten are the stages of a man's life. A full thousand is called ten hundreds. Pregnant women bear for ten months, and there are ten Erakas, ten Dasas, and ten Dasharnas."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"एकादशैकादशिनः पशूना-\nमेकादशैवात्र भवन्ति यूपाः ।\nएकादश प्राणभृतां विकारा\nएकादशोक्ता दिवि देवेषु रुद्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eleven are the eleven-fold animals, and there are eleven posts here. Eleven are the changes of living things, and in heaven among the gods eleven Rudras are spoken of."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"संवत्सरं द्वादश मासमाहु-\nर्जगत्याः पादो द्वादशैवाक्षराणि ।\nद्वादशाहः प्राकृतो यज्ञ उक्तो\nद्वादशादित्यान्कथयन्तीह विप्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A year is said to have twelve months. The Jagati metre has twelve syllables in a foot. The ordinary sacrifice is called the twelve-day one, and brahmins speak here of twelve Adityas."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"त्रयोदशी तिथिरुक्ता महोग्रा\nत्रयोदशद्वीपवती मही च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thirteenth lunar day is called most dreadful, and the earth has thirteen continents."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा विरराम बन्दी\nश्लोकस्यार्धं व्याजहाराष्टवक्रः ।\nत्रयोदशाहानि ससार केशी\nत्रयोदशादीन्यतिच्छन्दांसि चाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this much, Bandin stopped, and Ashtavakra completed the half-verse: \"Keshi ran for thirteen days, and the Vedas speak of metres beyond, beginning with thirteen.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो महानुदतिष्ठन्निनाद-\nस्तूष्णींभूतं सूतपुत्रं निशम्य ।\nअधोमुखं ध्यानपरं तदानी-\nमष्टावक्रं चाप्युदीर्यन्तमेव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a great shout arose, as the charioteer's son stood silent, his face downcast and lost in thought, while Ashtavakra went on speaking."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा संकुले वर्तमाने\nस्फीते यज्ञे जनकस्याथ राज्ञः ।\nअष्टावक्रं पूजयन्तोऽभ्युपेयु-\nर्विप्राः सर्वे प्राञ्जलयः प्रतीताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that stir, at King Janaka's rich sacrifice, all the brahmins approached Ashtavakra, honouring him, with joined hands and delighted."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"अनेन वै ब्राह्मणाः शुश्रुवांसो\nवादे जित्वा सलिले मज्जिताः किल ।\nतानेव धर्मानयमद्य बन्दी\nप्राप्नोतु गृह्याप्सु निमज्जयैनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is said that this man defeated learned brahmins in debate and drowned them in water. Let Bandin now meet that same fate. Seize him and drown him."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"अहं पुत्रो वरुणस्योत राज्ञ-\nस्तत्रास सत्रं द्वादशवार्षिकं वै ।\nसत्रेण ते जनक तुल्यकालं\nतदर्थं ते प्रहिता मे द्विजाग्र्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the son of King Varuna. There he held a twelve-year sacrificial session. Janaka, those chief brahmins were sent by me to match your own session in time."}},{"n":25,"text":"एते सर्वे वरुणस्योत यज्ञं\nद्रष्टुं गता इह आयान्ति भूयः ।\nअष्टावक्रं पूजये पूजनीयं\nयस्य हेतोर्जनितारं समेष्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"They have all gone to see Varuna's sacrifice and will come back here. I honour Ashtavakra, who deserves honour, because of whom I shall meet my father."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"विप्राः समुद्राम्भसि मज्जितास्ते\nवाचा जिता मेधया आविदानाः ।\nतां मेधया वाचमथोज्जहार\nयथा वाचमवचिन्वन्ति सन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those brahmins were drowned in the waters of the ocean, defeated in speech, though they were learned. By intelligence I have now drawn out that speech, as the good gather up words."}},{"n":27,"text":"अग्निर्दहञ्जातवेदाः सतां गृहा-\nन्विसर्जयंस्तेजसा न स्म धाक्षीत् ।\nबालेषु पुत्रेषु कृपणं वदत्सु\nतथा वाचमवचिन्वन्ति सन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fire, though it burns, sets free the houses of the good and does not consume them by its heat. So when young sons speak wretchedly, the good gather up their words."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्लेष्मातकी क्षीणवर्चाः शृणोषि\nउताहो त्वां स्तुतयो मादयन्ति ।\nहस्तीव त्वं जनक वितुद्यमानो\nन मामिकां वाचमिमां शृणोषि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do you hear, Janaka, with your splendour faded like a tree of the Shleshmataka? Or do praises intoxicate you? Tormented like an elephant, you do not hear this speech of mine."}},{"text":"जनक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janaka said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"शृणोमि वाचं तव दिव्यरूपा-\nममानुषीं दिव्यरूपोऽसि साक्षात् ।\nअजैषीर्यद्बन्दिनं त्वं विवादे\nनिसृष्ट एष तव कामोऽद्य बन्दी ॥","meaning":{"en":"I hear your speech of divine form, not human; you are a god in form. Since you defeated Bandin in debate, he is released to you today as you wish."}},{"text":"अष्टावक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"नानेन जीवता कश्चिदर्थो मे बन्दिना नृप ।\nपिता यद्यस्य वरुणो मज्जयैनं जलाशये ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I have no use for this Bandin alive. If his father is Varuna, then drown him in the water."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"अहं पुत्रो वरुणस्योत राज्ञो\nन मे भयं सलिले मज्जितस्य ।\nइमं मुहूर्तं पितरं द्रक्ष्यतेऽय-\nमष्टावक्रश्चिरनष्टं कहोडम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the son of King Varuna. I have no fear of being drowned in the water. In this very moment Ashtavakra will see his father Kahoda, lost long ago."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"ततस्ते पूजिता विप्रा वरुणेन महात्मना ।\nउदतिष्ठन्त ते सर्वे जनकस्य समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those brahmins, honoured by the great-souled Varuna, rose up near Janaka."}},{"text":"कहोड उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kahoda said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"इत्यर्थमिच्छन्ति सुताञ्जना जनक कर्मणा ।\nयदहं नाशकं कर्तुं तत्पुत्रः कृतवान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janaka, this is why people want sons: what I could not do, my son has done."}},{"n":34,"text":"उताबलस्य बलवानुत बालस्य पण्डितः ।\nउत वाविदुषो विद्वान्पुत्रो जनक जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"From a weak man a strong son is born, from a boy a learned one, and from an unlearned man a wise one, Janaka."}},{"text":"बन्द्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bandin said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"शितेन ते परशुना स्वयमेवान्तको नृप ।\nशिरांस्यपाहरत्वाजौ रिपूणां भद्रमस्तु ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"With your sharp axe, king, Death himself carries off the heads of your enemies in battle. May good come to you."}},{"n":36,"text":"महदुक्थ्यं गीयते साम चाग्र्यं\nसम्यक्सोमः पीयते चात्र सत्रे ।\nशुचीन्भागान्प्रतिजगृहुश्च हृष्टाः\nसाक्षाद्देवा जनकस्येह यज्ञे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great Ukthya is sung and the best Sama, and soma is properly drunk here at this session. The gods themselves, delighted, accepted their pure shares at Janaka's sacrifice here."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"समुत्थितेष्वथ सर्वेषु राज-\nन्विप्रेषु तेष्वधिकं सुप्रभेषु ।\nअनुज्ञातो जनकेनाथ राज्ञा\nविवेश तोयं सागरस्योत बन्दी ॥","meaning":{"en":"When all those brahmins had risen, shining brilliantly, King Janaka gave leave, and Bandin entered the waters of the ocean."}},{"n":38,"text":"अष्टावक्रः पितरं पूजयित्वा\nसंपूजितो ब्राह्मणैस्तैर्यथावत् ।\nप्रत्याजगामाश्रममेव चाग्र्यं\nजित्वा बन्दिं सहितो मातुलेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashtavakra honoured his father, and honoured by those brahmins as was fitting, having defeated Bandin, returned with his uncle to his own excellent hermitage."}},{"n":39,"text":"अत्र कौन्तेय सहितो भ्रातृभिस्त्वं\nसुखोषितः सह विप्रैः प्रतीतः ।\nपुण्यान्यन्यानि शुचिकर्मैकभक्ति-\nर्मया सार्धं चरितास्याजमीढ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descendant of Ajamidha, son of Kunti, here you have lived happily with your brothers, content among brahmins. Pure in deed and single in devotion, you have visited other holy places with me."}}]}]}